## Safe execution and proof

Before mutation: record outcome, constraints, live baseline, exact targets, one candidate and rollback. Run `sweep` with keyword and synonyms. An unavailable source is not zero matches. Reuse what exists. Claim the physical folder through `single-builder-guard.py` on every Codex turn that changes files; coordinate branch/deploy ownership without making Phil mediate. Keep builds and caches outside synced folders, preserve unrelated work, and stop task-created processes.

Read implementing code and the live service before asserting state. Source, branch, installed artifact and production are distinct. A registry stage, successful build, assignment or HTTP 200 cannot prove the customer path. Use `prepared`, `tested`, `published`, `installed`, `live`, and `sale-ready` precisely. Test the final delivered artifact and public front door, including relevant owner access, privacy and payment properties. Check the existing product ID, owning repo/branch and deployment account before editing; similar names are not proof of shared identity. See `OPERATING_AUTHORITY.md` for provenance and supersessions.

Completion scope is `v_product_completion` filtered by `active_for_completion AND NOT ghostwire_scope_excluded`. Name scope and query time with counts. `v_north_star` is a separate commercial KPI. GhostWire has separate release authority. Do not reactivate completed/frozen work from historical notes. Preserve explicit device acceptance until relevant conditions change. Inspect failures rather than repeating unchanged failed actions twice.

