- **Useful files only:** retain business originals, approved releases/fallbacks, unique/paid media and purposeful build backups, each with product, purpose, version/date and a restore manifest. Do not fill Drive with regenerable caches, disposable concatenations or duplicate downloads. File temporary intake at task closeout; no blind age-based deletion.
- **Security:** company root and new archives private by default; no anyone/domain-wide sharing. Preserve intentional customer delivery links. Keep credentials, signing keys, password exports, OAuth tokens and private recovery packs out of ordinary Drive; preserve owner access. Google Drive is not an independent offline backup.
- **Build preflight:** run `python3 storage/build-preflight.py --peak-gib N --workspace PATH` before large builds/downloads. Use actual additional peak space. Keep active source, dependencies, databases and emulator disks outside Drive/iCloud; use existing authorised remote compute when local capacity cannot fit, without new spending.
- Keep at least **25 GiB free on `/System/Volumes/Data`**. Before a large build or download, account for its peak additional local space; reclaim or archive eligible material first if it would consume that reserve. Continue unaffected work when a storage step is blocked.
- Keep active source checkouts, uncommitted work, current application state, signing keys, secrets, open files and required current/fallback artifacts local or in their existing protected custody. GitHub remains the backup for committed code; prove remote commit reachability and preserve untracked/ignored work before retiring a checkout. Never upload secrets, private recovery material or unrelated personal files to ordinary company Drive.
- Copy first, verify remote file sizes and cryptographic hashes/readback, retain a manifest plus a retrieval link or restore command, then release only the unchanged, verified local duplicate within the authorised scope. A queued sync or successful upload alone is insufficient. Keep archives cloud-only/on-demand; do not mirror the archive back onto the Mac. Deleting a file inside a synced Drive folder can delete the cloud copy too: use the supported local-only space-release action there.
- Clean up each lane's own inactive regenerable build output and temporary copies at closeout. Preserve concurrent work, existing guards and active releases. Do not kill daemons, reset the Mac or weaken protections to reclaim space.
- Cloud Drive provides storage, not build compute. Keep build scratch/caches outside synced folders; remote execution requires an already-authorised build service. Report measured free space and any remaining shortfall rather than declaring the 25 GiB target met merely because archives exist.

